{
 "code": "await rlm.harness.create_memory(title='ARC separator-grid four-corner agreement rule', content='For tiled ARC grids with regularly spaced separator rows/columns and color markers at their intersections, extract the intersection-marker matrix. The output has one cell per adjacent pair of separator rows and columns. Set output[r,c] to the shared value only if all four corner marker values for that rectangular block agree; otherwise use the uniform interior/background color (not necessarily separator color). Example task-ad47be90: intersection matrix rows [9,9,7,7,7], [9,9,7,0,0], [4,4,4,0,0], [4,4,4,8,8], [7,7,7,8,8] produced [[9,1,1,1],[1,1,1,0],[4,4,1,1],[1,1,1,8]], with interior background 1. A separate demo with background 6 confirmed mismatches map to 6 and unanimous 2/7/0 corners retain that value. Identify separator coordinates from repeating grid structure; ignore non-intersection regular line cells.",
 "global_": true,
 "metadata": {
  "task_family": "ARC tiled separator grids"
 }
}
